{
  "_comment": [
    "Shipping rates per product profile and destination.",
    "",
    "Every variant in content/shop/*.md names a shippingProfile. A basket may",
    "mix profiles (stickers plus a print, say); the customer is then charged the",
    "HIGHEST applicable rate once, not the sum, because the order ships together.",
    "",
    "Country codes are matched first. _EUROPE catches the remaining countries in",
    "the europe list below, _WORLD catches everything else.",
    "",
    "After editing, run:  node scripts/sync-worker-config.mjs",
    "then:                cd checkout-worker && npx wrangler deploy",
    "No Stripe key needed - rates are created inline per checkout, so nothing",
    "has to be registered in the Stripe dashboard.",
    "",
    "taxCode txcd_92010001 is Stripe's 'Shipping' code, so Stripe Tax applies the",
    "right rate to postage rather than guessing.",
    "",
    "shipTo lists every country checkout offers, as code → name. Because of the",
    "EU Packaging and Packaging Waste Regulation (PPWR) we currently do not ship",
    "to the EU/EEA. The cart dropdown is built from this list (src/lib/countries.ts)",
    "and the Worker refuses any country that is not on it.",
    "Left out although wanted, because Stripe Checkout cannot take a delivery",
    "address there: Cuba, Iran, Marshall Islands, Micronesia, Palau, Sudan, Syria."
  ],
